      "content": "/*\n    This program solves Laplace's equation on a regular 2D grid using simple Jacobi iteration.\n*/\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <time.h>\n#include <sys/time.h>\n\n#define CONV_THRESHOLD 1.0e-5f // threshold of convergence\n\n// Contiguous row-major working and auxiliary matrices.\ndouble *grid;\ndouble *new_grid;\n\n// size of each side of the grid\nint size;\nint iter_max_num;\n\n// return the absolute value of a number\ndouble absolute(double num){\n    if(num < 0)\n        return -1.0 * num;\n    return num;\n}\n\n// allocate memory for the grids\nvoid allocate_memory(){\n    if(size <= 0){\n        grid = NULL;\n        new_grid = NULL;\n        return;\n    }\n\n    const size_t n = (size_t)size;\n    if(n > SIZE_MAX / sizeof(*grid) / n)\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n\n    const size_t bytes = n * n * sizeof(*grid);\n    grid = (double *)malloc(bytes);\n    new_grid = (double *)malloc(bytes);\n    if(grid == NULL || new_grid == NULL){\n        free(grid);\n        free(new_grid);\n        exit(EXIT_FAILURE);\n    }\n}\n\n// initialize the grids, including identical fixed boundaries\nvoid initialize_grid(){\n    int center = size / 2;\n    int linf = center - (size / 10);\n    int lsup = center + (size / 10);\n    const size_t stride = (size_t)size;\n\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        const size_t row = (size_t)i * stride;\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            double value;\n            if(i >= linf && i <= lsup && j >= linf && j <= lsup)\n                value = 100;\n            else\n                value = 0;\n            grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\n            new_grid[row + (size_t)j] = value;\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n// save the grid in a file\nvoid save_grid(){\n    const size_t stride = (size_t)size;\n    for(int i = 0; i < size; i++){\n        const double *row = grid + (size_t)i * stride;\n        for(int j = 0; j < size; j++){\n            fprintf(stdout, \"%lf \", row[j]);\n        }\n        fprintf(stdout, \"\\n\");\n    }\n}\n\nint main(int argc, char *argv[]){\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &size);\n    fscanf(stdin, \"%d\", &iter_max_num);\n\n    int hasError = 1;\n    int iter = 0;\n    const size_t stride = (size_t)size;\n\n    allocate_memory();\n    initialize_grid();\n\n    // Each sweep reads only the current buffer and writes the next buffer.\n    while(hasError && iter < iter_max_num){\n        hasError = 0;\n        for(int i = 1; i < size - 1; i++){\n            const size_t offset = (size_t)i * stride;\n            const double *restrict current = grid + offset;\n            const double *restrict north = grid + offset - stride;\n            const double *restrict south = grid + offset + stride;\n            double *restrict next = new_grid + offset;\n            int rowHasError = 0;\n\n            for(int j = 1; j < size - 1; j++){\n                const double value = 0.25 * (current[j + 1] + current[j - 1] +\n                                             north[j] + south[j]);\n                next[j] = value;\n                const double errorCurrent = absolute(value - current[j]);\n                rowHasError |= (errorCurrent > CONV_THRESHOLD);\n            }\n            hasError |= rowHasError;\n        }\n\n        // Publish this iteration, including the iteration that converges.\n        double *temporary = grid;\n        grid = new_grid;\n        new_grid = temporary;\n        iter++;\n    }\n\n    save_grid();\n    free(grid);\n    free(new_grid);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/laplace_seq.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Contiguous ping-pong buffers should improve locality and eliminate copy-back traffic, while integer-OR convergence reduction makes the unit-stride stencil more SIMD-friendly.",
  "notes": "Preserves stencil addition order, threshold, stopping behavior and output formatting. Both buffers retain identical boundaries, including tiny grids. No commands or measurements performed.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Replace separately allocated rows with two contiguous row-major buffers.",
    "Initialize both buffers identically and swap them after every completed sweep instead of copying interiors.",
    "Use restricted row pointers and an integer-OR convergence reduction without reassociating floating-point additions."
  ]
